WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.028 --> 00:00:03.728
- [Narrator] This is the Pava Aliblanca,

00:00:03.728 --> 00:00:05.844
the bird that came back from extinction.

00:00:05.844 --> 00:00:08.205
(lively, bouncy music)

00:00:08.205 --> 00:00:10.645
The Pava Aliblanca is a slender black bird

00:00:10.645 --> 00:00:12.747
with a black tipped beak and nine large,

00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:16.137
white flight feathers
at the end of its wings.

00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:19.687
It was first discovered
in 1877, but after several

00:00:19.687 --> 00:00:22.515
research expeditions with no sightings,

00:00:22.515 --> 00:00:25.025
the Pava Aliblanca was declared extinct

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.185
by the scientific community.

00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:31.756
Then in 1977, the species
was rediscovered in Peru.

00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:34.223
With less than 250 known specimens,

00:00:34.223 --> 00:00:37.158
they are classified as
critically endangered.

00:00:37.158 --> 00:00:39.408
This is the Pava Aliblanca.

00:00:43.016 --> 00:00:45.183
(chiming)

